WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.050
Speaker 1: Welcome back, everybody, to the
David Pakman Show.

00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:03.050
My name is Luke Beasley.

00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:06.990
I'm going to be filling in for David today
while he is away on paternity leave.

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:09.400
Obviously exciting stuff going on.

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.769
Huge congratulations to David and his family.

00:00:11.769 --> 00:00:12.769
We will.

00:00:12.769 --> 00:00:13.800
Massive show to get into.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.669
So let's dove right in.

00:00:15.669 --> 00:00:20.100
Last night, the January 6th committee held
their first big public hearing where they

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:23.490
started the process of going through all of
the information they have gathered over the

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.730
last number of months.

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:30.130
And I thought that the chairman, Congressman
Thompson, as well as Liz Cheney, who kind

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:35.930
of led the presentation for the night, did
a really good job of outlining a few main

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:36.930
points.

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:40.520
So we're going to do a bird's eye view, look
at these main points, and then we're going

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:43.760
dove into some specific moments.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:50.800
The first is Donald Trump was absolutely supportive
and they made this very clear of the rioters.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:53.540
He was watching it unfold and he was supportive
of it.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:57.620
And as we're going to get into in just a second,
he was even.

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:05.370
CHEERING on, supportive of the rioters who
wanted to kill his own vice president.

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:10.650
The second big thing was he absolutely was
told by people close to him repeatedly that

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:12.230
the claims he was making were false.

00:01:12.230 --> 00:01:16.710
I think we had all kind of assumed that, but
that was shown as well.

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:20.850
People like former Attorney General William
Barr and his own daughter Ivanka Trump were

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:23.200
aware that the election was not stolen.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:24.570
There's no evidence for that.

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:27.820
And yet Trump kept perpetuating it.

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:34.790
The third big thing was there was a clear
and planned, coordinated effort to attack

00:01:34.790 --> 00:01:37.340
the Capitol by the Proud Boys and the Oath
Keepers.

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:42.040
And the reason why I say that is because there
was some question of was it just a protest

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:47.500
that got out of hand or was it a premeditated
event by some people?

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:52.030
And at least in the case of the Proud Boys
and the Oath Keepers, it was premeditated.

00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:54.050
And that's a big deal.

00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:59.950
The fourth big thing, and this is the most
important part of all of this is Donald Trump

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:04.960
was the first U.S. president in all of our
history to not respect the peaceful transition

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:05.960
of power.

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:11.650
And that is huge because that is absolutely
necessary to holding together our democracy.

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:15.520
And he just spit all over it because he was
just upset.

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:17.200
He lost an election.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:21.110
He stomped on our entire history of doing
a really good job.

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:25.000
The person who's in power, if they lose, they
respectfully exit and do what they can to

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.360
make it a peaceful transition.

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:29.700
And so that put our democracy in peril.

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:35.080
And that's a huge point we have to keep stating
so that everyone does not forget it.

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:38.569
Obviously, these videos can't be super, super
long, so I can't go through everything that

00:02:38.569 --> 00:02:43.209
I would want to from this hearing because
there was a lot jam packed into it.

00:02:43.209 --> 00:02:46.921
The stuff that I can't cover, I'll try to
get to some of it on my own show so you can

00:02:46.921 --> 00:02:49.470
find that at Luke Beazley on YouTube.

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:52.970
If you're watching this on YouTube or listening
to the podcast, it'll be in the description

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:58.600
box, a link to my channel, but definitely
check out my show, Luke Beazley on YouTube.

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:02.830
But I also encourage you to watch the whole
hearing if you haven't already yourself, because

00:03:02.830 --> 00:03:07.110
there is tons of stuff there, super, super
important for you to be aware of that came

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:09.069
out of that hearing.

00:03:09.069 --> 00:03:17.550
So the first humongous bombshell that came
out of this hearing was it was exposed that

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:22.770
Donald Trump was supportive of the rioters
who were chanting, chanting, hang Mike Pence.

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:26.990
He was made aware that that was happening
and he was supportive of it.

00:03:26.990 --> 00:03:27.990
Let's take a look.

00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:31.770
Speaker 2: And aware of the rioters chants
to hang Mike Pence.

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:37.740
The president responded with this sentiment,
quote, Maybe our supporters have the right

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:38.740
idea.

00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:40.800
Mike Pence, quote, deserves it.

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:44.860
Speaker 1: I know because there's already
been coverage of a lot of this and you've

00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:46.190
priority right through your head.

00:03:46.190 --> 00:03:49.050
You know numbed out to it but really think
about this.

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:54.900
The president of the United States was supportive
of a mob of people who wanted to murder his

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:56.180
vice president.

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:57.180
You would watch that?

00:03:57.180 --> 00:03:58.180
A movie like.

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:00.410
That's not even something that would be fiction,
right?

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:05.570
If you ever heard that story, the fictional
know, the president of the United States wanted

00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:06.780
his vice president to get murdered.

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:08.380
That's what we just watched.

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:11.160
And we can't forget that these crazy things
happen or get numbed out to them.

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:17.499
The next big thing I want to look at is William
Barr, Trump's attorney general, testified

00:04:17.499 --> 00:04:23.419
in a prerecorded interview about how he looked
into it, saw there is no fraud that would

00:04:23.419 --> 00:04:28.059
have made any difference in the election,
no wide scale widespread fraud.

00:04:28.059 --> 00:04:32.839
And then we'll play the clip of Ivanka who
got asked about Barr's statement and pretty

00:04:32.839 --> 00:04:35.229
much said, Yeah, I mean.

00:04:35.229 --> 00:04:36.779
If Barr said it like I believe it.

00:04:36.779 --> 00:04:39.759
So pretty much I don't agree with my dad's
statements.

00:04:39.759 --> 00:04:41.210
Let's take a look.

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:49.430
Speaker 3: Told the president in no uncertain
terms that I did not see evidence of fraud.

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:55.740
And, you know, that would have affected the
outcome of the election.

00:04:55.740 --> 00:05:01.181
And frankly, a year and a half later, I haven't
seen anything to change my mind on that.

00:05:01.181 --> 00:05:06.860
How did that affect your perspective about
the election when Attorney General Barr made

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:07.979
that statement?

00:05:07.979 --> 00:05:10.490
It affected my perspective.

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:14.199
I respect Attorney General Barr.

00:05:14.199 --> 00:05:18.840
So I. Accepted what he was saying.

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:24.819
Speaker 1: So Donald Trump's attorney general
and his daughter are both well aware.

00:05:24.819 --> 00:05:32.509
And William Barr told Trump that Trump's claims
were false and yet he kept on going with them.

00:05:32.509 --> 00:05:37.499
And the amount of damage that that did, if
he had stopped at some point before January

00:05:37.499 --> 00:05:42.289
6th and realized, you know what, I thought
I was dying, but looks like all the evidence

00:05:42.289 --> 00:05:43.289
has come out.

00:05:43.289 --> 00:05:44.289
It was actually stolen.

00:05:44.289 --> 00:05:49.460
We would have saved so much damage from being
done to our democracy.

00:05:49.460 --> 00:05:54.830
The next big thing that happened in the hearing
was a documentarian testified under oath.

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:58.360
And again, I encourage you guys to go watch
this hearing for yourself, but I'll give you

00:05:58.360 --> 00:05:59.360
a quick summary.

00:05:59.360 --> 00:06:04.211
So the documentarian had been allowed access
in the days leading up to January 6th and

00:06:04.211 --> 00:06:10.190
on January 6th to follow around Enrique Tarrio,
who is the leader of the Proud Boys.

00:06:10.190 --> 00:06:13.990
And throughout that, I guess they wanted him
or were okay with him making a documentary

00:06:13.990 --> 00:06:19.300
about the organization or whatever was going
on and what he captured and witnessed throughout

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:24.539
that process proved what I mentioned earlier
that the proud boys, in coordination with

00:06:24.539 --> 00:06:29.189
the Oath Keepers, had actually planned the
events of that day.

00:06:29.189 --> 00:06:32.659
And we're just executing a plan to attack
the Capitol.

00:06:32.659 --> 00:06:36.129
We'll look at some clips from that testimony
that came out.

00:06:36.129 --> 00:06:40.279
Speaker 4: On January 5th, the night before
the attack.

00:06:40.279 --> 00:06:46.469
You were with the head of the Proud Boys,
Mr. Tarrio in Washington, D.C..

00:06:46.469 --> 00:06:47.469
What happened?

00:06:47.469 --> 00:06:53.710
Speaker 5: We picked up his bags and went
to get some other bags from the Phenix Hotel.

00:06:53.710 --> 00:06:59.279
We encountered Mr. Stuart Rhodes from the
Oath Keepers.

00:06:59.279 --> 00:07:07.029
We drove down into the parking garage and
filmed the scene of Mr. Tarrio and Mr. Rhodes

00:07:07.029 --> 00:07:11.619
and certain other individuals in that garage.

00:07:11.619 --> 00:07:16.020
Speaker 3: The committee learned that the
Oath Keepers set up quick reaction forces

00:07:16.020 --> 00:07:19.409
outside of the city in Virginia, where they
stored arms.

00:07:19.409 --> 00:07:23.629
The goal of these quick reaction forces was
to be on standby just in case President Trump

00:07:23.629 --> 00:07:25.059
invoked the Insurrection Act.

00:07:25.059 --> 00:07:28.000
Did the Coopers ever provide weapons to members?

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:30.039
I'm going to climb to answer that.

00:07:30.039 --> 00:07:31.199
If that's the grounds.

00:07:31.199 --> 00:07:35.689
Speaker 1: They're acting as if they're executing
some military operation.

00:07:35.689 --> 00:07:42.110
So after the documentarian spoke, a female
police officer recounted her experience trying

00:07:42.110 --> 00:07:44.459
desperately to defend the Capitol.

00:07:44.459 --> 00:07:47.979
And one of the stories she tells, she's holding
one of those bike racks that doubles as a

00:07:47.979 --> 00:07:51.999
fence and she gets shoved backwards, hits
her head on a rail and then onto the cement

00:07:51.999 --> 00:07:53.690
and gets knocked out cold.

00:07:53.690 --> 00:07:58.219
So she goes through and walks through that
and then walks through the other traumatizing,

00:07:58.219 --> 00:08:02.400
horrible things that happened and that she
witnessed that day.

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:05.569
That kind of brings me to my last big point
on this.

00:08:05.569 --> 00:08:08.139
My baseline emotion watching all of this was
just rage.

00:08:08.139 --> 00:08:11.960
At the beginning, I thought about this a lot
before, but at the beginning, because they

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:17.319
pointed out it was top of mind for me that
we have this long history of peaceful transition

00:08:17.319 --> 00:08:18.849
of power.

00:08:18.849 --> 00:08:23.860
And while you and I both know some horrible
things have happened in American history,

00:08:23.860 --> 00:08:26.810
we've failed miserably in the past many times.

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:31.959
But the one thing we got right was that peaceful
transition of power and is what kept our democracy

00:08:31.959 --> 00:08:34.320
alive.

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:44.130
And Donald Trump was willing to let that all
die, to let democracy in America die.

00:08:44.130 --> 00:08:45.130
For his own gain.

00:08:45.130 --> 00:08:46.270
For his own benefit.

00:08:46.270 --> 00:08:50.820
Because he wanted more to believe he won and
to stay in power than just admitting he lost

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:56.650
the election and moving along like every other
president had done in the past.

00:08:56.650 --> 00:09:00.240
That's a fact we cannot let people lose sight
of.

00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:03.500
That's how deeply selfish and narcissistic
he is.

00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:07.580
He doesn't care about the greater good of
the country because if he did, he would have

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:10.800
realized the claims he was making were false.

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:16.190
And then conceded and helped to make a peaceful
transition of power.

00:09:16.190 --> 00:09:18.330
But that's not what he did.

